<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Asunción</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asuncion">Asunción</a> was signed on 26 March 1991 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> in the Paraguayan capital. It created <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercosur">Mercosur</a>, the Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">Common Market</a>, committing the four states to free movement of goods and a common external tariff, and it built on earlier rapprochement between Argentina and Brazil after their return to democracy.</p></div>
